  "details": "I have yet to see a post about this, and the only one that seems like it could be is over shadowing the actual problem some of us are experiencing, I made a recent post in the locomotion layer bug post and realized later that was not my problem\n its simple to explain and also very specific.\nwhen I load certain avatars that are not within the proper t pose or fbx pose when i uploaded them, the head becomes shifted, unless in vr, or unless i turn off dynamic bones completely, im positive you guys did something for when avatars load, before you seemed to use an animation to lock in the viewball on avatar load (not just in fullbody you dont see it happen in 3 point tracking) that animation SEEMED to be tpose-new which is featured in sdk 2\nI experimented and fixed an avatar that had A SERIOUS problem with having dynamic bones on the head and the chest which caused it to warp because it was also in a very messed up bicycle pose in unity, however it always uploaded fine because of MY THEORY being that it places it into tpose-new then locks the viewball then you start tracking, i ALWAYS use tpose new as a reference to where i place the viewball and alot of fbx poses were unreliable which is why i even think this is what happens\nno i have no evidence that confirms this but years of testing and results being accurate to what am even theorizing is telling enough\nANYWAYS , the problem allegedly persists within dynamic bone exclusions being messed up along with how the viewball is being locked into place on avatar load\nim sure some people are experiencing your viewball being in the wrong spot or head tilting. \nhttps://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/811432780214566932/847296878571683870/unknown.png\nhttps://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/811432780214566932/847296975719235665/unknown.png\nhttps://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/811432780214566932/847297016446976070/unknown.png\nthese are three models of effect with dynamic bones not limited to zero ON DESKTOP\nif i limit the bones, and then load them again with NO DYNAMICS they still have a head tilt\nTHAT IS UNTIL I GET INTO AT LEAST 3 POINT TRACKING VR\ni recently fixed my 3.0 version of the avatar in the first picture by forcing it out of the weird bicycle pose and into , yes, the anim t pose new within my 3.0 scene. \nit completely fixed it on desktop and vr\nas seen here \nhttps://media.discordapp.net/attachments/811432780214566932/847297713112481792/unknown.png?width=1246&height=701\nNOW THIS IS WHERE IT GETS CONFUSING!!!!\nthe 3.0 pramanix avatar used to warp on the ground ( i do not have pictures of it now ) \nkinda like how that bug when you are prone and you open your menu and no matter what your prone is you seem to stand on your feet with your head in the same spot as if you have your head up your own butt... lol maybe another canny post is suitable for that\nanyways yeah in vr if i moved my head it would warp all over the area in pivot to my viewpoint way above the avatar warping into itself on the ground from this bug.\nanywho this is how specific and weird this bug is, it fixed itself on DESKTOP as well UNLIKE THE OTHERS, when i switched off dynamic bones.\nyeah this is very confusing and i dont understand it at all and i really wish that the locomotion problem didnt overshadow this, currently the workaround for using dynamic bones limiter to turn them off then load in vr is a good workaround but you have to turn the dynamics off then reload the avatar then turn them back on if you want dynamic bones so im just going without them for now, however  i cant even stand around in the first three models mentioned in desktop so its a nuisance\ni hope my really strung out post helps people \ntldr : the head on some models and some bodies are messing up if they arent in a proper pose when uploading from unity when they have dynamic bones directly on stuff like the head, and chest, it seems exclusions \"breaking\" might be the cause of this cause turning off dynamic bones fixes this in most cases.  \n\nwhat im more curious about is how many of these avatars you guys are getting reports for in the locomotion thread actually route to this bug and NOT the locomotion layer.\n\n\navatar id's in order from appearance : \npramanixkITE : avtr_6d7300eb-b6d1-4980-85fe-9f2319568e54\nvalvatorez/nosferatu : avtr_ed03e598-3be2-4963-87aa-7438a8d66721\nenciodas/silverash : avtr_46ef310a-198d-4c36-ba48-aed6a866284a\nand pramanix 3.0 is here but its fixed now, you might just have to load 1 update ago to check that condition cause i fixed it last update using the t-posenew workaround pose : avtr_f3bd69f5-bfe2-43f5-88fc-662dc1b8561d\nand no it doesnt even matter if these use rig hacks or not, but if you must know \nvalvatorez/nosferatu and enciodas/silverash do NOT use any form of rig hacks.\nthank you thank you thank you thank you",
